OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F310A1786724321
OL,3,CFour killed in Japan after record-
OL,4,Cbreaking rainfall floods homes and
OL,5,Croads
OL,7,FThe prefecture said four people had
OL,8,Fdied, including a man found on a
OL,9,Fflooded road in Ichikawa city and a
OL,10,Fwoman who was stuck in a flooded car
OL,11,Fin Sakura city.
OL,13,FAnother person was pulled from a
OL,14,Fflooded car in Kashiwa City.
OL,16,FMore than 80 homes were flooded in the
OL,17,Fprefecture, and nearly 230,000
OL,18,Fresidents were advised to take
OL,19,Fshelter, Chiba officials said.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G2/6
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
